   "t": 0.06666666666666667,
   "dur": 5.317,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Which hand aged? In four and a half years, one showed no detectable ageing."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 6.366666666666666,
   "dur": 10.944,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "They belong to two neighbours in Nambour, a Queensland town where pure chance decided who would wear sunscreen every morning. Head, neck, arms and hands, before the day began."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 18.5,
   "dur": 10.291,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "It was never sunscreen against none: the others could use it whenever they pleased, or not at all. Researchers read the fine lines in silicone casts of hands."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 29.7,
   "dur": 10.076,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "It's easy to think sun damage is the burn you feel. But an ultraviolet camera reveals damage the naked eye misses, long before it shows on the surface."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 42.3,
   "dur": 9.589,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "And they were followed for ten more years. Melanoma, the most serious skin cancer, came out at about half, in numbers too small to be sure."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 55.36666666666667,
   "dur": 5.809,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "At a lab's test dose, that morning layer is about a fifth of a paper's thickness."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 62.36666666666667,
   "dur": 6.251,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "So, which hand aged? Both groups missed mornings; one missed fewer, and the skin kept count."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 69.83333333333333,
   "dur": 4.586,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: tanning beds share a list with cigarettes. Same list, same risk?"
  }
 ]
}